<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Home Assistant card components</title>
    <%= renderTemplate("../../../src/html/_header.html.template") %>
    <meta name="referrer" content="same-origin" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no"
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#03a9f4" />
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        --page-background: #fafafa;
        --page-text: #212121;
        --page-code-background: #e5e5e5;
        --page-divider: #dddddd;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root:not([data-scheme="light"]) {
          color-scheme: dark;
          --page-background: #111111;
          --page-text: #e1e1e1;
          --page-code-background: #1c1c1c;
          --page-divider: #333333;
        }
      }
      :root[data-scheme="dark"] {
        color-scheme: dark;
        --page-background: #111111;
        --page-text: #e1e1e1;
        --page-code-background: #1c1c1c;
        --page-divider: #333333;
      }
      html {
        background-color: var(--page-background);
        color: var(--page-text);
      }
      body {
        font-family: Roboto, Noto, sans-serif;
        -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        line-height: 1.5;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0 16px 64px;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 880px;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 32px 0 8px;
      }
      h2 {
        margin: 48px 0 8px;
      }
      pre {
        background: var(--page-code-background);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 12px 16px;
        overflow-x: auto;
        font-size: 13px;
      }
      code {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      }
      table {
        border-collapse: collapse;
        width: 100%;
      }
      th,
      td {
        text-align: start;
        vertical-align: top;
        padding: 8px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--page-divider);
      }
      .cards {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
        gap: 16px;
        align-items: start;
        margin: 16px 0;
      }
      .single {
        max-width: 400px;
        margin: 16px 0;
      }
      .log {
        height: 160px;
        overflow-y: auto;
        margin: 0;
      }
      button {
        font: inherit;
        padding: 6px 12px;
        margin-inline-end: 8px;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Home Assistant card components</h1>
      <p>
        Embed working Home Assistant dashboard cards in any page. The cards run
        against a mocked backend in the browser. No Home Assistant server is
        necessary.
      </p>
      <p>There are two components:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>&lt;ha-embed-provider&gt;</code> holds the mocked backend and
          its entities.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>&lt;ha-embed-card&gt;</code> renders one card. It uses the
          backend of a provider.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All cards in the same provider share their entities. When you change
        an entity in one card, the other cards show the change.
      </p>

      <p>
        Color scheme of this page and its cards:
        <button data-scheme="">Auto</button>
        <button data-scheme="light">Light</button>
        <button data-scheme="dark">Dark</button>
      </p>

      <h2>Use on your site</h2>
      <p>
        Load the script from the demo site. The script loads all other files
        from the demo site too.
      </p>
      <pre><code>&lt;script type="module" src="https://demo.home-assistant.io/embed.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>

      <h2>One card</h2>
      <p>
        Put the entities in a script tag inside the provider. Put the card
        configuration in a script tag inside the card. Both take JSON with
        <code>type="application/json"</code> or YAML with
        <code>type="text/yaml"</code>. The card configuration is the same as in
        a dashboard. YAML needs its indentation. If your site minifies HTML,
        make sure the minifier keeps the whitespace in script tags, or use
        JSON.
      </p>
      <pre><code>&lt;ha-embed-provider&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/yaml"&gt;
    - entity_id: light.kitchen
      state: "on"
      attributes:
        friendly_name: Kitchen
        supported_color_modes: [brightness]
        color_mode: brightness
        brightness: 180
  &lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;ha-embed-card&gt;
    &lt;script type="text/yaml"&gt;
      type: tile
      entity: light.kitchen
      tap_action:
        action: toggle
      features:
        - type: light-brightness
    &lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;/ha-embed-card&gt;
&lt;/ha-embed-provider&gt;</code></pre>
      <ha-embed-provider>
        <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
          - entity_id: light.kitchen
            state: "on"
            attributes:
              friendly_name: Kitchen
              supported_color_modes: [brightness]
              color_mode: brightness
              brightness: 180
        </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
        <div class="single">
          <ha-embed-card>
            <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
              type: tile
              entity: light.kitchen
              tap_action:
                action: toggle
              features:
                - type: light-brightness
            </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
          </ha-embed-card>
        </div>
      </ha-embed-provider>
      <p>
        The <code>entities</code> attribute of the provider and the
        <code>config</code> attribute of the card also take JSON.
      </p>

      <h2>Cards with shared state</h2>
      <p>
        These three cards are in one provider. Turn on a light in one card. The
        other cards update. The log below shows the events of the provider.
      </p>
      <ha-embed-provider id="shared">
        <script type="application/json">
          [
            {
              "entity_id": "light.living_room",
              "state": "off",
              "attributes": {
                "friendly_name": "Living room",
                "supported_color_modes": ["brightness"],
                "color_mode": "brightness",
                "brightness": 255
              }
            },
            {
              "entity_id": "switch.coffee_maker",
              "state": "on",
              "attributes": {
                "friendly_name": "Coffee maker",
                "device_class": "outlet"
              }
            },
            {
              "entity_id": "climate.hallway",
              "state": "heat",
              "attributes": {
                "friendly_name": "Hallway",
                "current_temperature": 19.5,
                "temperature": 21,
                "min_temp": 7,
                "max_temp": 30,
                "target_temp_step": 0.5,
                "hvac_modes": ["heat", "off"],
                "hvac_action": "heating",
                "supported_features": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "entity_id": "sensor.outside_temperature",
              "state": "12.3",
              "attributes": {
                "friendly_name": "Outside temperature",
                "device_class": "temperature",
                "state_class": "measurement",
                "unit_of_measurement": "°C"
              }
            }
          ]
        </script>
        <div class="cards">
          <ha-embed-card>
            <script type="application/json">
              {
                "type": "tile",
                "entity": "light.living_room",
                "tap_action": { "action": "toggle" }
              }
            </script>
          </ha-embed-card>
          <ha-embed-card>
            <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
              type: entities
              title: Living room
              entities:
                - light.living_room
                - switch.coffee_maker
                - sensor.outside_temperature
            </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
          </ha-embed-card>
          <ha-embed-card>
            <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
              type: thermostat
              entity: climate.hallway
            </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
          </ha-embed-card>
        </div>
      </ha-embed-provider>
      <pre class="log" id="log"><code>Use the cards to see events here.</code></pre>

      <h2>Cards outside a provider</h2>
      <p>
        A card does not have to be inside a provider. A card outside a provider
        uses the first provider on the page. Put one provider with all entities
        at the top of the page, and put the cards anywhere below it. If the
        page has no provider, the card adds an empty provider to the page.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use a different provider, set the <code>provider</code> attribute of
        the card to the ID of the provider.
      </p>
      <pre><code>&lt;ha-embed-provider id="living-room"&gt;…&lt;/ha-embed-provider&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some text about the coffee maker.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ha-embed-card provider="living-room"&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/yaml"&gt;
    type: tile
    entity: switch.coffee_maker
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/ha-embed-card&gt;</code></pre>
      <p>
        These two cards are not inside a provider. The first card uses the
        first provider on this page, the kitchen light at the top. The second
        card uses the provider with the ID <code>shared</code> above.
      </p>
      <div class="cards">
        <ha-embed-card>
          <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
            type: tile
            entity: light.kitchen
            tap_action:
              action: toggle
          </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
        </ha-embed-card>
        <ha-embed-card provider="shared">
          <!-- htmlmin:ignore --><script type="text/yaml">
            type: tile
            entity: switch.coffee_maker
            tap_action:
              action: toggle
          </script><!-- htmlmin:ignore -->
        </ha-embed-card>
      </div>

      <h2>Light and dark mode</h2>
      <p>
        The cards follow the light or dark mode of the browser. To choose the
        mode, set the <code>color-scheme</code> attribute of the provider to
        <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>. Use this when your site has its
        own switch for dark mode. The buttons at the top of this page do this.
        The cards keep their styles inside. They do not change the styles of
        your page.
      </p>
      <pre><code>&lt;ha-embed-provider color-scheme="dark"&gt;…&lt;/ha-embed-provider&gt;</code></pre>

      <h2>Change entities from the page</h2>
      <p>
        Set the <code>entities</code> property to change entities from
        JavaScript. The new list replaces all entities. To change one entity,
        start from the current states.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button id="set-temperature">Set a random outside temperature</button>
        <button id="toggle-coffee">Toggle the coffee maker</button>
      </p>
      <pre><code>const provider = document.querySelector("ha-embed-provider");
provider.entities = Object.values(provider.hass.states).map((entity) =&gt;
  entity.entity_id === "sensor.outside_temperature"
    ? { ...entity, state: "18.1" }
    : entity
);</code></pre>
      <p>
        To use the actions of an entity, call a service. The provider updates
        the state and the cards.
      </p>
      <pre><code>provider.hass.callService("switch", "toggle", {
  entity_id: "switch.coffee_maker",
});</code></pre>

      <h2>Listen to changes</h2>
      <p>
        The provider fires a <code>states-changed</code> event when the state
        of one or more entities changes. The event has the states of all
        entities. The event bubbles.
      </p>
      <pre><code>provider.addEventListener("states-changed", (ev) =&gt; {
  const { states } = ev.detail;
  console.log(states["light.living_room"].state);
});</code></pre>
      <p>
        Read the current state of all entities with
        <code>provider.hass.states</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Custom cards</h2>
      <p>
        Custom cards work too. Load the script of the custom card on the page,
        and use <code>custom:</code> and the element name as the card type.
        The custom card gets the same mocked backend as the other cards.
        <code>window.loadCardHelpers()</code> is available to create built-in
        cards.
      </p>
      <p>
        The mocked backend only knows a part of the Home Assistant API. A
        custom card that asks for history, statistics, or templates gets an
        error. From another site, the script of the custom card needs CORS
        headers, like the embed script.
      </p>
      <pre><code>&lt;script type="module" src="https://example.com/embed-demo-custom-card.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;ha-embed-card&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/yaml"&gt;
    type: custom:embed-demo-custom-card
    entity: light.office
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/ha-embed-card&gt;</code></pre>
      <ha-embed-provider>
        <script type="application/json">
          [
            {
              "entity_id": "light.office",
              "state": "on",
              "attributes": {
                "friendly_name": "Office",
                "supported_color_modes": ["brightness"],
                "color_mode": "brightness",
                "brightness": 120
              }
            }
          ]
        </script>
        <div class="single">
          <ha-embed-card
            config='{ "type": "custom:embed-demo-custom-card", "entity": "light.office" }'
          ></ha-embed-card>
        </div>
      </ha-embed-provider>
      <p>This is the code of the custom card:</p>
      <pre><code>class EmbedDemoCustomCard extends HTMLElement {
  setConfig(config) {
    if (!config.entity) {
      throw new Error("Set an entity");
    }
    this._config = config;
  }

  set hass(hass) {
    this._hass = hass;
    this._render();
  }

  getCardSize() {
    return 3;
  }

  async _render() {
    if (!this.shadowRoot) {
      this.attachShadow({ mode: "open" }).innerHTML = `
        &lt;style&gt;
          ha-card { padding: 16px; }
          .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 2px 8px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            background: var(--accent-color);
            color: var(--text-accent-color, #fff);
            font-size: 12px;
          }
          .tile { margin: 12px 0; }
        &lt;/style&gt;
        &lt;ha-card&gt;
          &lt;span class="badge"&gt;Custom card&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;
            This is a custom card. It is not part of Home Assistant. The page
            defines it, and it creates the tile card below with the card
            helpers.
          &lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;div class="tile"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;button&gt;Toggle from the custom card&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/ha-card&gt;`;
      this.shadowRoot.querySelector("button").addEventListener("click", () =&gt;
        this._hass.callService("homeassistant", "toggle", {
          entity_id: this._config.entity,
        })
      );
    }
    // Keep the promise, so that a second update does not create a second tile.
    if (!this._tile) {
      this._tile = window.loadCardHelpers().then((helpers) => {
        const tile = helpers.createCardElement({
          type: "tile",
          entity: this._config.entity,
        });
        this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".tile").append(tile);
        return tile;
      });
    }
    (await this._tile).hass = this._hass;
  }
}

customElements.define("embed-demo-custom-card", EmbedDemoCustomCard);</code></pre>
      <script type="module">
        class EmbedDemoCustomCard extends HTMLElement {
          setConfig(config) {
            if (!config.entity) {
              throw new Error("Set an entity");
            }
            this._config = config;
          }

          set hass(hass) {
            this._hass = hass;
            this._render();
          }

          getCardSize() {
            return 3;
          }

          async _render() {
            if (!this.shadowRoot) {
              this.attachShadow({ mode: "open" }).innerHTML = `
                <style>
                  ha-card { padding: 16px; }
                  .badge {
                    display: inline-block;
                    padding: 2px 8px;
                    border-radius: 8px;
                    background: var(--accent-color);
                    color: var(--text-accent-color, #fff);
                    font-size: 12px;
                  }
                  .tile { margin: 12px 0; }
                </style>
                <ha-card>
                  <span class="badge">Custom card</span>
                  <p>
                    This is a custom card. It is not part of Home Assistant. The page
                    defines it, and it creates the tile card below with the card
                    helpers.
                  </p>
                  <div class="tile"></div>
                  <button>Toggle from the custom card</button>
                </ha-card>`;
              this.shadowRoot.querySelector("button").addEventListener("click", () =>
                this._hass.callService("homeassistant", "toggle", {
                  entity_id: this._config.entity,
                })
              );
            }
            // Keep the promise, so that a second update does not create a second tile.
            if (!this._tile) {
              this._tile = window.loadCardHelpers().then((helpers) => {
                const tile = helpers.createCardElement({
                  type: "tile",
                  entity: this._config.entity,
                });
                this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".tile").append(tile);
                return tile;
              });
            }
            (await this._tile).hass = this._hass;
          }
        }

        customElements.define("embed-demo-custom-card", EmbedDemoCustomCard);
      </script>

      <h2>Reference</h2>
      <h3><code>&lt;ha-embed-provider&gt;</code></h3>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>entities</code></td>
          <td>Attribute and property</td>
          <td>
            A list of entities. Each entity has an <code>entity_id</code>, a
            <code>state</code>, and <code>attributes</code>. The optional keys
            <code>area_id</code>, <code>device_id</code>, and
            <code>platform</code> set the entity registry entry. A new list
            replaces all entities. A JSON or YAML script child sets the first
            list.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>color-scheme</code></td>
          <td>Attribute and property (<code>colorScheme</code>)</td>
          <td>
            <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>. Without it, the cards
            follow the browser setting.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>hass</code></td>
          <td>Property, read-only</td>
          <td>The mocked Home Assistant object that the cards use.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>states-changed</code></td>
          <td>Event</td>
          <td>
            Fires when the state of one or more entities changes. The detail
            has <code>states</code>, the states of all entities by entity ID.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <h3><code>&lt;ha-embed-card&gt;</code></h3>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>config</code></td>
          <td>Attribute and property</td>
          <td>
            The card configuration, the same as in a dashboard. A JSON or YAML
            script child sets the first configuration.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>provider</code></td>
          <td>Attribute and property</td>
          <td>
            The ID of the provider to use. Without it, the card uses the
            provider around it, else the first provider on the page.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>
        The mocked backend knows the actions of lights, switches, climate,
        covers, fans, locks, media players, and more. Actions that open dialogs,
        such as <code>more-info</code>, do nothing.
      </p>
    </main>
    <script>
      (function () {
        var shared = document.getElementById("shared");
        var log = document.getElementById("log");
        var first = true;
        shared.addEventListener("states-changed", function (ev) {
          var states = ev.detail.states;
          var line =
            new Date().toLocaleTimeString() +
            "  " +
            Object.keys(states)
              .map(function (entityId) {
                return entityId + "=" + states[entityId].state;
              })
              .join(", ");
          if (first) {
            log.textContent = "";
            first = false;
          }
          log.textContent = line + "\n" + log.textContent;
        });
        document
          .getElementById("set-temperature")
          .addEventListener("click", function () {
            var states = shared.hass.states;
            shared.entities = Object.keys(states).map(function (entityId) {
              var entity = states[entityId];
              return {
                entity_id: entityId,
                state:
                  entityId === "sensor.outside_temperature"
                    ? (Math.random() * 30 - 5).toFixed(1)
                    : entity.state,
                attributes: entity.attributes,
              };
            });
          });
        document
          .querySelectorAll("button[data-scheme]")
          .forEach(function (button) {
            button.addEventListener("click", function () {
              var scheme = button.getAttribute("data-scheme");
              if (scheme) {
                document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-scheme", scheme);
              } else {
                document.documentElement.removeAttribute("data-scheme");
              }
              document
                .querySelectorAll("ha-embed-provider")
                .forEach(function (provider) {
                  if (scheme) {
                    provider.setAttribute("color-scheme", scheme);
                  } else {
                    provider.removeAttribute("color-scheme");
                  }
                });
            });
          });
        document
          .getElementById("toggle-coffee")
          .addEventListener("click", function () {
            shared.hass.callService("switch", "toggle", {
              entity_id: "switch.coffee_maker",
            });
          });
      })();
    </script>
    <%= renderTemplate("../../../src/html/_js_base.html.template") %>
    <%= renderTemplate("../../../src/html/_script_loader.html.template") %>
  </body>
</html>
